Behaviours to know

Rounding: “Round up” means ceiling. Fe at 2 moles gives 111.69 g, which shows as 112, and ΔH of -890.3 shows as -890, since rounding up moves toward positive. If you want normal rounding instead, change ceil to round in format_number.
Floating-point errors: format_number rounds to 4 decimals before taking the ceiling. Without that, 111.69 g of Fe is about 2.0000000000000004 mol and would show as 3.
Stoichiometry: it isn’t affected, because balanced coefficients are always whole numbers already.

